WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:03.760
- We're back with our Moms
Timeout, our first one ever,

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:05.810
with Janna, whose story went viral

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:08.800
after posting this pic of her son Ezra,

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:13.210
very frustrated on his first
day of virtual kindergarten.

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:15.990
It's heartbreaking, we all
related, it went viral.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:18.710
And, we're just talking about being moms,

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:21.030
and you're trying to do it all

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:24.960
and doing your best and
holding your families together

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.150
during these times.

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:28.050
And I hope that anyone out there

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:30.940
who may be watching who's
going through this, too,

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:33.920
can just join in on this conversation,

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:38.920
because we're all trying
to juggle all of this.

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:42.010
How are you doing?
- A juggling act, for sure.

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:43.253
- How are you doing it?

00:00:45.256 --> 00:00:47.630
- Ironically, my kids give me my strength.

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:48.510
They're my why.

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:50.242
They're my reason.

00:00:50.242 --> 00:00:51.075
And they're my whole world,

00:00:51.075 --> 00:00:52.990
even though motherhood is
like the hardest journey ever,

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:55.470
like you said, I wouldn't
have it any other way.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:58.260
So I think we're just
taking one day at a time.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:01.680
And some days you are doing great

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:03.420
and other days it's a challenge,

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:05.180
but you just have to take it day by day,

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:06.860
and give yourself a lot of grace.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:10.920
- You said that really your kids,

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:13.680
while being the thing that sort of has to,

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:18.680
you have to give the most
life force to and output wise,

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:23.930
is the thing that gives you
the strength in order to do it.

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:24.980
And again, I'm just like,

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:26.480
that's what I'm talking about, Jana.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:28.410
You say things in this way

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:32.070
that just make a relatable
light bulb go off.

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:32.903
- Thank you.

00:01:32.903 --> 00:01:35.090
I think, like you said, all
moms can relate to that,

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:38.400
that they're our why,
they're our driving force.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.080
- Well, I think that you've
done a tremendous thing

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:45.760
for people because we
feel better when we know

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:47.620
we're all in the boat together,

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:52.410
rather than in lonely
little canoes, disconnected.

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:55.880
And I thought yours was
so selfless and relatable.

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:57.820
And this is sort of, to me,

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:02.820
like the example of how
powerful sharing can be.

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:03.693
- Thank you so much.

00:02:03.693 --> 00:02:04.680
That means a lot.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:07.170
And that was the whole reason
behind sharing this photo

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:09.550
was I knew that, like I said,

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:12.067
all along that I'm not
gonna be the only one

00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:13.690
going through this,

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:15.600
but seeing someone else post it,

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:17.266
and whether that's myself,

00:02:17.266 --> 00:02:19.330
it just resonates with so many families

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:21.200
and that we just don't want
to feel alone in all of this,

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.670
'cause it can be a lonely time.

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:24.980
- May I ask what you said to Ezra

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:27.390
when you did see him crying?

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:28.800
You took the picture-
- Yeah.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:31.410
- But then what was your,

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:32.960
what was your follow through, may I ask?

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:34.123
What's your advice?

00:02:35.046 --> 00:02:36.950
- So I asked him to step
away from the computer,

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:37.910
and he came over by me,

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:40.040
and we actually sat on
the floor and just hugged.

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:41.220
And we both had tears,

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:43.830
but I told him that it's
not just hard for him.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.010
It's hard for everybody,

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:46.590
that we're gonna get
through this together,

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:48.080
and that we're gonna just try our best,

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:49.990
but it was still really hard for him

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:51.550
to understand that this was his reality,

00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:52.840
that it's gonna be on the computer,

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:53.930
because even the night before

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:56.560
he was sticking his shoes
out for the next day.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:00.270
- I love that you said, let's
step away and take a break.

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:02.870
I think kids and adults can really benefit

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:05.560
from that kind of separation.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:08.380
It changes and shifts our energy.

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:10.830
I mean, you're such a good mom, Jana.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:13.060
What do you do to take care of yourself?

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:13.893
What do you do?

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:14.726
How do you,

00:03:14.726 --> 00:03:15.850
how do you,

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:17.713
I know we all put our kids first,

00:03:17.713 --> 00:03:20.580
but do you get to do things for yourself?

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:22.550
You're such a good mom.

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:23.680
- Oh, thank you.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:25.130
So having four kids obviously

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:27.040
that leaves a lot less time for myself,

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.590
but before kids,

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:30.840
I was a competitive figure skater

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:32.190
and then turned coach.

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:35.320
So that was a huge part of my life.

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:39.460
And now where we live
the rink is an hour away.

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:41.410
With Atlanta traffic
it's even more than that.

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:43.630
So it's not reality for me right now,

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:46.900
but I hope to spark that passion
back in my life sometime.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:48.570
- Oh gosh, yeah,

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:52.120
I think that would be
an amazing prescription

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:53.840
of getting back to,

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:57.680
also physical exertion is so positive

00:03:57.680 --> 00:03:59.950
for the mental state
and the physical state,

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:02.740
for taking on all that you do as a mom.

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:04.220
God, I wanna get you back

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:07.270
and find time for you to figure skate.

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:08.970
- That would be amazing.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:10.380
It's a huge hole in my heart right now,

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:13.320
but that's all right, because
there'll be time for it.

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:17.480
- Yeah, well, we have
a Moms Timeout surprise

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:22.480
called The PolyGlide Synthetic Ice Company

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:26.003
is gonna put a rink in your backyard.

00:04:26.003 --> 00:04:26.875
- [Audience Member] What?

00:04:26.875 --> 00:04:28.620
(audience cheering)
- What?

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:30.020
I'm like in shock right now.

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:35.980
- Apparently they just put one
in Justin Bieber's backyard,

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:36.813
so,

00:04:38.230 --> 00:04:39.751
they know what they're doing.

00:04:39.751 --> 00:04:41.810
(audience cheering)
- Wow.

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:45.470
- Yeah, and I can't thank-
- Thank you.

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:46.940
That's amazing.

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:48.310
- You deserve this.

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:51.140
And I wish that we could
all wave a magic wand

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:52.500
for one another.

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:57.500
And we were all so excited
and cheering and freaking out

00:04:57.610 --> 00:04:58.443
that we could-

00:04:58.443 --> 00:04:59.810
- My kids are gonna freak out.

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:02.969
- I know, they can use it, too.

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:04.430
- Yes.

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:07.340
- But this one's all about you, Jana.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:09.110
You really deserve this.
- Thank you.

00:05:09.110 --> 00:05:11.990
- Thank you for making
us all feel less alone,

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:15.190
more connected, and relate to each other.

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:17.020
I think your approach and your advice

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:19.100
and your tactics are fantastic.

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:21.140
And would it be okay if we,

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:24.870
once we built the skate
rink in your backyard,

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:26.970
we can come visit and like check it out

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:28.713
and see how it's going for you?

00:05:29.950 --> 00:05:31.480
- Please, that would be amazing.

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:33.160
- Okay, all right (laughing).

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:34.670
Well you give us all strength

00:05:34.670 --> 00:05:37.110
and we'll be checking back in on

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:38.760
how the progress is going

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:42.799
on your brand new ice skating
rink in your backyard.

00:05:42.799 --> 00:05:44.901
(audience cheering)

00:05:44.901 --> 00:05:46.160
- That's so cool.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:48.632
- Well, thank you, Jana, so much.

00:05:48.632 --> 00:05:51.215
(upbeat music)

